{"chunk_id": "142329d36f71", "text": "After threatening Sita, the enraged Ravana orders a band of grotesque demonesses to break her spirit. They drag the despairing princess to the Ashoka grove, a lush but prison-like garden where she will be guarded, threatened, and coaxed into yielding to him. Surrounded by terrifying watchers, Sita collapses in grief, remembering Rama and Lakshmana. Meanwhile, Rama\u2014having slain the shape-shifting demon Maricha disguised as a deer\u2014hurries back to the hermitage. Ominous signs fill the forest: jackals howl, beasts cry, and birds move ominously to his left. Realizing that Maricha\u2019s dying imitation of his voice may have lured Lakshmana away, Rama fears a trap. When he finally sees Lakshmana returning alone, his anxiety deepens, and he reproaches him, convinced that terrible harm may have befallen Sita.\nAfter killing the demon Maricha, Rama hurries back to the hermitage, troubled by ominous portents and fearing Sita has been harmed.\nThemes: ominous portents, anxiety for Sita, demonic deception, brotherly tension", "vector": [0.0004123923717997968, -0.024140864610671997, 0.010263239033520222, 0.006257743574678898, -0.019892610609531403, 0.023048456758260727, -0.027890115976333618, -0.017438065260648727, -0.01271104160696268, -0.01645354926586151, 0.020445559173822403, 0.006881495006382465, 0.012771731242537498, 0.02198302187025547, -0.0005558973643928766, 0.0015054324176162481, 0.054350659251213074, -0.0037155351601541042, 0.04202398657798767, -0.017343660816550255, -0.0060756755992770195, 0.014646356925368309, 0.0017599903512746096, 0.0009052823879756033, -0.021564939990639687, -0.006153223104774952, 0.00397852249443531, -0.04013587161898613, 0.014201302081346512, 0.0014599154237657785, -0.01433616690337658, -0.028240764513611794, -0.003014236455783248, -0.0122727295383811, -0.025772731751203537, 0.004305570386350155, 0.0004429477558005601, -0.014943060465157032, 0.0041235024109482765, -0.001704358495771885, 0.00238205